    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0353" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d239-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-20">November 20, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the President from Secretary Hull</p>
                <p>Ankara reports on November 18 that Numan
                    obtained approval of Party Leaders to reply to Eden that Turks have now decided in principle to enter the war.
                        Numan agreed that military assistance
                    to Turkey is now the prime consideration and political question of Russian <pb
                        facs="0354" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/> assurances should be postponed. British
                    believe Turkish decision cannot long remain secret and are concerned about
                    possible premature Axis attack. British evacuated about 1,000 troops from Leros
                    to Turkey, but reported to have lost seven destroyers.</p>
                <p>Ankara reports on November 17 that Von
                        Papen told Finnish Minister that Turks will not enter War.
                    Minister believes Von Papen intends to
                    reassure Hitler and, while concealing
                    truth from Hitler, hasten his downfall as
                        Von Papen stated peace was not
                    possible unless<anchor n="2" xml:id="d239-f2"/>
                    Hitler and the Nazis were removed from
                    power.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the White House Map Room to Greer
                    at Oran, apparently via military channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d239-f2" n="2" xml:id="d239-f2-content">
                <p>This reads “unless and until” in the file copy in the Hull Papers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
